<title>USA: Transco files shelf for $300 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Transco files shelf for $300 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transcontinental Gas Pipe Line Corp, a unit of The Williams Cos, filed Friday with the Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf registration to sell up to $300 million in debt securities.  </p>
<p>Proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, including repayment of outstanding debt, the Houston-based company said.</p>
<p>Transco, owns and operates a 10,000 mile pipeline system that runs from stations in south Texas and Louisiana to New York.</p>
</text>
